WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.331 --> 00:00:04.642
Stay optimistic!

00:00:04.820 --> 00:00:06.940
If you want to achieve success as an entrepreneur

00:00:07.095 --> 00:00:11.075
you have to stay optimistic that it’s going to work out.

00:00:11.075 --> 00:00:13.299
Because life is going to throw you curve balls

00:00:13.299 --> 00:00:14.864
you’re going to make a lot of mistakes

00:00:14.864 --> 00:00:16.322
you might lose a lot of money

00:00:16.322 --> 00:00:18.823
you’re going to have the #LITTLEMAN in your life

00:00:18.823 --> 00:00:21.842
tell you all the reasons why your idea’s not going to work out.

00:00:22.537 --> 00:00:26.197
You need to stay optimistic that it will.

00:00:26.642 --> 00:00:28.861
One of my favorite stories is of Walt Disney.

00:00:28.993 --> 00:00:31.911
When he was a little boy his father beat him regularly.

00:00:31.911 --> 00:00:35.454
That was his form of, I don’t know

00:00:35.786 --> 00:00:36.984
getting rid of some aggression.

00:00:37.318 --> 00:00:38.744
But he took it out on his son Walt.

00:00:39.243 --> 00:00:42.094
And at a really young age Walt started drawing

00:00:42.094 --> 00:00:43.555
and doodling.

00:00:43.825 --> 00:00:46.077
And his life at home sucked

00:00:46.478 --> 00:00:48.231
and instead of getting down on himself

00:00:48.231 --> 00:00:49.784
he remained optimistic

00:00:49.784 --> 00:00:51.909
and created this fantasyland for himself

00:00:51.909 --> 00:00:54.355
where he imagined he was playing and living.

00:00:54.729 --> 00:00:57.285
When he got a little bit older the war was on

00:00:57.285 --> 00:00:58.210
and so he joined the army.

00:00:58.314 --> 00:01:00.588
He went and he was an ambulance driver in France.

00:01:01.306 --> 00:01:02.901
And all he saw around him was people

00:01:02.901 --> 00:01:04.496
with their limbs being blown off

00:01:04.496 --> 00:01:07.051
and blood everywhere and just misery.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.747
And he was the ambulance driver, right,

00:01:09.747 --> 00:01:12.504
imagine how much bad stuff you see every day.

00:01:12.824 --> 00:01:14.259
And he remained optimistic

00:01:14.639 --> 00:01:16.584
and he wanted people to be happy.

00:01:16.584 --> 00:01:20.011
And so how do you be happy if you’re being picked up by an ambulance?

00:01:20.672 --> 00:01:23.812
And the little touch that he added was he would draw cartoons

00:01:24.313 --> 00:01:27.868
and sketches all over his ambulance of happy creatures

00:01:28.529 --> 00:01:29.880
and people having a good time

00:01:30.178 --> 00:01:31.936
to try to uplift people’s spirits.

00:01:32.338 --> 00:01:34.780
He remained optimistic even in the hardest circumstances.

00:01:35.829 --> 00:01:38.020
He came back to America and he wanted to start his own business.

00:01:38.020 --> 00:01:38.902
He wanted to be an animator.

00:01:38.902 --> 00:01:41.852
He wanted to create his own creations and share it with the world.

00:01:42.615 --> 00:01:44.994
And it got so hard for him that he was in Kansas City

00:01:45.229 --> 00:01:47.397
and he couldn’t afford to have an apartment anymore

00:01:47.604 --> 00:01:49.264
so he slept at his office.

00:01:49.432 --> 00:01:50.648
He lived at his office.

00:01:50.850 --> 00:01:52.843
He ate cold beans every day

00:01:52.843 --> 00:01:54.506
because he couldn’t afford real food.

00:01:54.906 --> 00:01:57.629
But he remained optimistic that it was going to work out.

00:01:58.300 --> 00:01:59.567
And then finally,

00:01:59.567 --> 00:02:03.134
finally after all this crap that happened to him

00:02:03.134 --> 00:02:04.988
after all these failures

00:02:05.388 --> 00:02:07.242
and not seeing any momentum or success

00:02:07.242 --> 00:02:09.096
he finally has something thing that takes off

00:02:09.447 --> 00:02:11.563
and it was Mortimer the Lucky Rabbit.

00:02:11.979 --> 00:02:13.232
That was his first creation

00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:14.925
that really had this commercial success.

00:02:15.885 --> 00:02:19.409
And he made the pivotal mistake of agreeing

00:02:19.945 --> 00:02:21.568
to allow the copyrights for

00:02:21.568 --> 00:02:24.541
Mortimer the Lucky Rabbit to go to his distributor

00:02:24.571 --> 00:02:26.885
and then his distributor cut him out of the deal

00:02:27.155 --> 00:02:28.961
and he lost his first creation.

00:02:30.499 --> 00:02:31.925
And instead of getting down on himself

00:02:31.925 --> 00:02:33.351
he remained optimistic.

00:02:33.351 --> 00:02:34.779
He thought it was going to work out.

00:02:35.232 --> 00:02:37.152
And he thought back to the times

00:02:37.152 --> 00:02:38.282
when he was in Kansas City

00:02:38.282 --> 00:02:40.623
in his office sitting on his cold floor

00:02:41.252 --> 00:02:42.608
and there was a pack of mice

00:02:42.608 --> 00:02:44.954
that were always hanging around in his office

00:02:44.954 --> 00:02:46.922
and one of them became a really

00:02:46.922 --> 00:02:49.180
close friend of Disney

00:02:49.180 --> 00:02:50.860
and he treated him as a pet.

00:02:51.672 --> 00:02:54.829
And so Walt Disney said, “You know what, my next creation

00:02:54.948 --> 00:02:56.100
I’m going to make it a mouse.”

00:02:56.922 --> 00:02:58.677
And it became Mickey Mouse.

00:02:59.468 --> 00:03:00.608
He remained optimistic,

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.614
he remained positive that it would work out

00:03:03.853 --> 00:03:06.837
and eventually it did even though he got pounded

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:09.622
and beat down and got screwed over

00:03:09.782 --> 00:03:12.484
and saw such terrible things in his life

00:03:12.484 --> 00:03:15.188
he remained optimistic that it will work out.

00:03:15.774 --> 00:03:17.922
One of my favorite quotes that Disney said

00:03:17.922 --> 00:03:19.926
just shortly before he died was

00:03:20.298 --> 00:03:22.813
“I hate to see downbeat pictures.

00:03:23.313 --> 00:03:27.168
I know life isn’t that way and I don’t want anyone telling me it is.

00:03:27.926 --> 00:03:28.832
So stay optimistic

00:03:29.438 --> 00:03:31.139
and believe that it’s going to work out.

